### Hero Shell Components (Progressive Loading)

For instant image loading on detail pages, use shell components that only need the media ID:

```tsx
import { HeroBackdropShell, HeroLogoShell } from "@/components/features/media";

// Renders immediately using CDN URLs - no data fetch needed
<HeroBackdropShell
  itemId={movieId}
  mediaType="movie"
  title="Loading..."  // Fallback alt text
  priority
>
  <HeroLogoShell
    itemId={movieId}
    mediaType="movie"
    title="Loading..."  // Fallback text if no logo
    priority
  />
</HeroBackdropShell>
```

**HeroBackdropShell** - Client component for backdrop images:
- Uses CDN URL: `https://image.themoviebrowser.com/{type}/{id}/backdrop.webp`
- Falls back to TMDB `backdrop_path` if CDN fails
- Handles gradient overlays (light/medium/heavy/none)
- Accepts children for content overlay

**HeroLogoShell** - Client component for logo images:
- Uses CDN URL: `https://image.themoviebrowser.com/{type}/{id}/logo.webp`
- Falls back to TMDB logo via `tmdbLogoPath` prop
- Falls back to text title if no logo available
- Three-state loading: cdn → tmdb → text

**Key pattern:** These components work with just `itemId` and `mediaType` (available from URL params), enabling instant image loading before the data fetch completes.

### Hero Section Architecture

The hero sections use a **unified, composable architecture** for visual consistency between homepage carousel and detail pages:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ HeroCarousel (landing page)    │ MediaHero (detail pages)   │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│            Aspect-Ratio Container (shared specs)            │
│  aspect-[16/9] md:aspect-[2.2/1] lg:aspect-[2.5/1]         │
│  max-h-[65vh] overflow-hidden                               │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                    MediaBackdrop                            │
│  (handles backdrop image positioning, gradients, overlays)  │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│          Content Overlay (absolute inset-0 z-10)           │
│          flex flex-col justify-end                          │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                     HeroContent                             │
│  (logo, genres, ratings, watch options - bottom aligned)    │
│  pb-5 md:pb-6 lg:pb-8 max-w-xl lg:max-w-2xl                │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
│                                                             │
│  MediaActionBar (separate component, below hero)            │
│  Play Trailer, Watchlist, Like/Dislike, Share              │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

#### Unified Container Structure

**CRITICAL**: Both `HeroCarousel` and `MediaHero` MUST use identical container specs for seamless transitions.

The hero uses CSS variables (defined in `globals.css`) for easily tweakable responsive sizing:

```css
/* globals.css - Hero Section Layout Variables */
:root {
  /* Hero height constraints */
  --hero-height-target: 60vh;
  --hero-height-min: 400px;
  --hero-height-max: 800px;
  --hero-height-mobile-target: 50vh;
  --hero-height-mobile-min: 300px;
  --hero-height-mobile-max: 500px;
  
  /* Hero content width (desktop): target 30vw, min 280px, max 480px */
  --hero-content-width-target: 30vw;
  --hero-content-min-width: 280px;
  --hero-content-max-width: 480px;
  
  /* Mobile content width: target 85vw, min 260px, max 400px */
  --hero-content-mobile-width-target: 85vw;
  --hero-content-mobile-min-width: 260px;
  --hero-content-mobile-max-width: 400px;
}

/* Hero container uses height-based sizing with max-height cap */
.hero-container {
  width: 100%;
  height: clamp(
    var(--hero-height-mobile-min),
    var(--hero-height-mobile-target),
    var(--hero-height-mobile-max)
  );
}

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .hero-container {
    height: clamp(
      var(--hero-height-min),
      var(--hero-height-target),
      var(--hero-height-max)
    );
    max-height: 60vh;  /* Cap at 60% of viewport */
  }
}
```

**Key design decisions:**
- Height-based sizing ensures hero never takes more than 60% of viewport
- `clamp()` provides smooth responsive behavior between min/max bounds
- Image positioning (`objectPosition: "85% 20%"`) shows top-right of image to preserve important content

```tsx
// Container uses .hero-container class for CSS variable-based height
<div className="hero-container relative w-full overflow-hidden">
  <MediaBackdrop ... className="absolute inset-0" />
  
  {/* Content overlay - positioned at bottom */}
  <div className="absolute inset-0 z-10 flex flex-col justify-end px-4 md:px-8 lg:px-12">
    {/* HeroContent uses .hero-content-width class for CSS variable-based width */}
    <HeroContent ... className="pb-5 md:pb-6 lg:pb-8" />
  </div>
</div>
```

**Why CSS variables with clamp()?** 
- Easily tweak min/max/target values in one place
- Uses `clamp(min, target, max)` for responsive sizing with hard limits
- Prevents hero from becoming too short on small screens or too tall on large screens
- Content width scales with viewport but respects readability bounds

#### Shared Components

**`MediaBackdrop`** / **`HeroBackdropShell`** - Prime Video-style backdrop:
- Image positioned to the right: `left-0 md:left-[18%] lg:left-[25%]`
- `object-cover` with `objectPosition: "85% 20%"` - 85% from left (right bias), 20% from top (shows more top of image)
- Black background base for clean left gradient fade
- Gradient fade from black on image's left edge (35-50% width)
- Subtle bottom gradient (10-28% height depending on overlay intensity)
- Three overlay presets: `light`, `medium`, `heavy`
- MUST have `h-full` on children wrapper for flexbox to work

**`HeroContent`** - Content layout (bottom-aligned):
- Uses `.hero-content-width` class for responsive width (30vw desktop, 85vw mobile with min/max)
- Logo (with responsive constraints: `max-w-[220px] md:max-w-[420px] lg:max-w-[520px]`)
- Gap between logo and info: `mb-4 md:mb-6 lg:mb-8`
- Genres → Ratings → Watch Options (compact vertical stack)
- Shared animation variants (`heroContainerVariants`, `heroItemVariants`)
- **No actions prop** - actions moved to separate `MediaActionBar`

**`MediaActionBar`** - Action buttons (separate from hero):
- Play Trailer, Watchlist toggle, Like/Dislike, Share
- Positioned between hero and overview with negative margin
- `className="px-4 md:px-8 lg:px-12 -mt-8 md:-mt-10 lg:-mt-12 relative z-20"`

```tsx
import { MediaHero, MediaActionBar } from "@/components/features/media";

// Detail page usage:
<MediaHero item={movie} mediaType="movie" />
<MediaActionBar
  itemId={movie.id}
  mediaType="movie"
  title={movie.title}
  trailer={trailer}
  className="px-4 md:px-8 lg:px-12 -mt-8 md:-mt-10 relative z-20"
/>
<MediaOverview item={movie} mediaType="movie" />

// HeroCarousel (landing page) - uses heroEnhancedData from getTrending()
<HeroCarousel
  items={trending.allItems}
  heroEnhancedData={trending.heroEnhancedData}  // Ratings + watch options per item
/>
```

#### Design Specs

- **Container**: `aspect-[16/9] md:aspect-[2.2/1] lg:aspect-[2.5/1] max-h-[65vh]`
- **Content positioning**: `flex flex-col justify-end` with bottom padding
- **Content max-width**: `max-w-xl lg:max-w-2xl` (prevents text spanning full width)
- **HeroCarousel**: Fully clickable (navigates to detail page)
- **Action buttons**: Glassmorphism style (`bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 backdrop-blur-sm`)

### RatingsBar Component

Unified ratings display showing scores from multiple sources (TMDB, IMDb, Rotten Tomatoes, Google).

```tsx
import { RatingsBar } from "@/components/features/media";

// Basic usage with ratings from movie/series
<RatingsBar ratings={movie.ratings} size="md" />

// Fallback to TMDB-only when no external ratings
<RatingsBar
  ratings={movie.ratings?.length
    ? movie.ratings
    : [{ name: "TMDB", rating: Math.round(movie.vote_average * 10).toString() }]
  }
/>
```

**Design principles:**
- Single grouped pill container (not separate pills per source)
- Ratings separated by subtle `border-white/15` dividers
- Icon + color-coded score for each source
- Muted color palette: `hsl(h, 50%, 55%)` for scores
- Sizes: `sm` (cards), `md` (hero), `lg` (detail sections)

**Vertical alignment pattern:**
```tsx
// Use fixed-height wrapper for icons to ensure alignment
<div className={cn("relative flex-shrink-0", heightClass)} style={{ width: iconSize }}>
  <Image src={icon} fill className="object-contain" unoptimized />
</div>
```

**Rating sources (in order):**
1. TMDB - Always shown first
2. IMDb - From MongoDB external_data
3. Rotten Tomatoes (Critic) - With certified/rotten variants
4. Rotten Tomatoes (Audience) - With certified/rotten variants
5. Google - From MongoDB googleData

### WatchOptions Component

Compact pill showing streaming providers for a movie/series:

```tsx
import { WatchOptions } from "@/components/features/media";

<WatchOptions
  watchOptions={item.watch_options}           // Pre-processed for user's country
  watchProviders={item.watch_providers}       // Raw TMDB data for country switching
  googleData={googleData}                     // Scraped data (India only)
  item={{ id, title, poster_path, backdrop_path, images }}
  isMovie={true}
/>
```

**Design specs:**
- Compact pill design with glassmorphism (`bg-black/30 backdrop-blur-sm`)
- Provider icons at 24x24px with tooltips for details
- Shows "Watch (IN)" indicator when using fallback country
- Max 5 providers visible, expand button for more

**Data flow:**
1. Server pre-processes watch options using `getWatchOptionsForCountry()`
2. Server also sends optimized `watch_providers` (filtered to ~15 countries)
3. Client re-processes on-the-fly when user changes country via `CountrySelector`
4. For JustWatch links (TMDB), opens Google search instead of broken deep links

**Integration in HeroContent:**
```tsx
// HeroContent receives watch props and renders WatchOptions after RatingsBar
<HeroContent
  watchOptions={watch_options}
  watchProviders={optimized_watch_providers}
  googleData={googleData}
  item={item}
  // ... other props
/>
```

### CountrySelector Component

Dropdown for selecting watch provider region:

```tsx
import { CountrySelector } from "@/components/features/layout";

// In NavBar
<CountrySelector />

// Compact mode (flag only)
<CountrySelector compact />
```

**Features:**
- Uses `country-list` library for complete country list (250+ countries)
- Priority countries (IN, US, UK, CA, AU, DE, FR, JP) shown at top
- Searchable with flag icons from `flagcdn.com`
- Stores selection in `countryOverride` (Zustand user store)
- Client-side only (not persisted to server)

**Design specs:**
- Button: Flag icon + country code (e.g., 🇮🇳 IN)
- Popover: 260px wide, 300px scroll area
- Search input at top for filtering

### NavBar Patterns

The navbar uses scroll-aware styling with compact, left-aligned elements:

**Search Button (Compact):**
```tsx
// Small button with search icon + keyboard shortcut (not a wide search bar)
<button onClick={() => setSearchOpen(true)} className="...">
  <Search className="h-4 w-4" />
  <kbd className="hidden lg:inline-flex h-5 ...">
    {isMac ? "⌘" : "Ctrl"}K
  </kbd>
</button>
```

**Scroll-Aware Styling:**
```tsx
// Nav items adapt to scroll state (transparent vs solid background)
<Button
  variant="ghost"
  className={cn(
    "gap-2",
    isScrolled
      ? "text-foreground/80 hover:text-foreground hover:bg-accent"
      : "text-white/90 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/10",
    pathname?.startsWith(href) && (isScrolled ? "bg-accent" : "bg-white/10")
  )}
>
```

**Right-Side Elements:**
- Compact search button (icon + shortcut)
- Country selector
- **Auth users**: UserMenu (includes card display + theme toggle in Appearance submenu)
- **Non-auth users**: SettingsMenu (cog icon) + Sign In button

**Settings Toggle Locations:**
- **Card Display**: Top of Appearance submenu (Poster Cards / Wide Cards)
- **Theme Mode**: Below card display (Light / Dark / System)
- **Color Theme**: Below mode (Default / Midnight Blue / Forest Green)

| Setting | Auth Users | Non-Auth Users |
|---------|------------|----------------|
| Card Display | UserMenu → Appearance | SettingsMenu |
| Theme Mode | UserMenu → Appearance | SettingsMenu |
| Color Theme | UserMenu → Appearance | SettingsMenu |

### Media Detail Page Patterns

#### Card Sizes in Scrollers

Consistent card widths across scrollable sections:

```tsx
// Standard poster cards (recommendations, similar, collection)
className="w-[130px] sm:w-[145px] md:w-[160px] flex-shrink-0"

// Cast cards (slightly smaller)
className="w-[110px] sm:w-[125px] md:w-[140px] flex-shrink-0"

// Gallery image thumbnails
style={{ height: "120px", width: `${aspectRatio * 120}px` }}
```

#### Modal Patterns: Dialog vs Custom Overlay

**Use shadcn Dialog for:**
- Detail views (episode details, login, search results)
- Content that needs structured layout with header/body/footer
- Views that benefit from focus trapping and accessibility

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD: Dialog for detail views
<Dialog open={isOpen}>
  <DialogContent className="sm:max-w-[95vw] lg:max-w-5xl">
    {/* Two-column layout, info cards, scrollers */}
  </DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

**Override shadcn Dialog default width:**
The default `sm:max-w-lg` must be overridden with sm breakpoint:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: Won't work - default sm:max-w-lg takes precedence
<DialogContent className="max-w-6xl">

// ✅ GOOD: Override at sm breakpoint
<DialogContent className="sm:max-w-[95vw] md:max-w-[90vw] lg:max-w-5xl">
```

**Use custom fixed overlay for:**
- Full-screen image lightboxes
- Video players
- Content that should cover the entire viewport

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD: Custom full-screen overlay for lightbox
{isOpen && (
  <div className="fixed inset-0 z-50 bg-black">
    <Button onClick={handleClose} className="absolute right-4 top-4 z-50">
      <X />
    </Button>
    {/* Full-screen image */}
  </div>
)}
```

Remember to prevent body scroll for custom overlays:

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (isOpen) {
    document.body.style.overflow = "hidden";
  } else {
    document.body.style.overflow = "";
  }
  return () => { document.body.style.overflow = ""; };
}, [isOpen]);
```

#### Video Gallery with YouTube Integration

The VideoGallery component displays YouTube videos with rich metadata from the YouTube Data API.

**Component Structure:**
```
src/components/features/media/
├── video-gallery.tsx      # Main gallery component
├── video-stats.tsx        # Stats display (views, likes, comments, channel)
└── video-comments.tsx     # Comments section with expand/collapse
```

**Features:**
- Batch fetches metadata for all videos on mount (up to 50 per API call)
- Fetches full data (stats + 100 comments) for active video
- Shows view count, comment count, like/dislike bar, channel info
- Comments in a card with show more/less toggle
- Sidebar at 25% width with video thumbnails

**Stats Row Layout:**
```tsx
// Views • Comments • Like/Dislike bar (all inline)
<div className="flex items-center gap-4">
  <div className="flex items-center gap-3 text-muted-foreground">
    <div className="flex items-center gap-1">
      <Eye className="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
      <span className="text-xs font-medium">{formatViewCount(viewCount)}</span>
    </div>
    <div className="flex items-center gap-1">
      <MessageCircle className="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
      <span className="text-xs font-medium">{formatViewCount(commentCount)}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <InlineLikeBar likes={likeCount} dislikes={dislikeCount} />
</div>
```

**Comments Card Pattern:**
```tsx
// Collapsed: 1 comment + "Show more" button
// Expanded: Scrollable list with all comments (up to 100)
<div className="rounded-lg bg-muted/30 overflow-hidden">
  {!isExpanded ? (
    <>
      <CommentItem comment={firstComment} />
      <Button onClick={() => setIsExpanded(true)}>Show more</Button>
    </>
  ) : (
    <ScrollArea className="h-[250px]">
      {comments.map(comment => <CommentItem key={comment.id} comment={comment} />)}
    </ScrollArea>
  )}
</div>
```

**Utility Functions** (`src/lib/youtube-utils.ts`):
```typescript
formatDuration(iso8601: string): string;     // "PT2M27S" → "2:27"
formatRelativeTime(dateString: string): string;  // "6 years ago"
formatViewCount(count: number): string;      // "350.7K", "3.8M"
```

#### Video Gallery Height Sync

Sync sidebar scroll area height with main player:

```tsx
const mainPlayerRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
const [playerHeight, setPlayerHeight] = useState(0);

useEffect(() => {
  const updateHeight = () => {
    if (mainPlayerRef.current) {
      setPlayerHeight(mainPlayerRef.current.offsetHeight);
    }
  };
  updateHeight();
  window.addEventListener("resize", updateHeight);
  return () => window.removeEventListener("resize", updateHeight);
}, []);

// Sidebar at 25% width
<div className="w-[25%] min-w-[280px] max-w-[400px] flex-shrink-0">
  <ScrollArea style={{ height: `${playerHeight + 60}px` }}>
```

#### Inline Video Playback

Videos should play in-place, not in modals:

```tsx
const [isPlaying, setIsPlaying] = useState(false);

{isPlaying ? (
  <iframe
    src={`https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/${videoKey}?autoplay=1&rel=0`}
    allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media"
    allowFullScreen
    className="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full"
  />
) : (
  <>
    <Image src={thumbnailUrl} fill />
    <button onClick={() => setIsPlaying(true)}>
      <Play />
    </button>
  </>
)}
```

