### Media Badges System

A unified badge system for displaying contextual labels on movie/series cards (e.g., "New", "Trending", "Acclaimed").

#### Architecture

```
src/lib/badges/
├── index.ts          # Export hub + universal getMediaBadges(), getHoverCardBadges(), getBadgeScoopColor()
├── types.ts          # BadgeType, MediaBadge, BadgeOptions
├── constants.ts      # BADGE_THRESHOLDS, BADGE_DEFINITIONS (70% opacity colors)
├── movie-badges.ts   # Movie-specific badge logic
├── series-badges.ts  # Series-specific badge logic
└── utils.ts          # Date helpers, badge creation utilities, getBadgeScoopColor()
```

#### Usage

```tsx
import { getMediaBadges, getHoverCardBadges, getBadgeScoopColor } from "@/lib/badges";

// Universal getter (auto-detects movie vs series)
const badges = getMediaBadges(item, { maxBadges: 1 });

// For hover card with minimal data
const badges = getHoverCardBadges(hoverData, isMovie, { maxBadges: 2 });

// In MovieCard/WideMovieCard
const badge = useMemo(
  () => (showBadges ? getMediaBadges(item, { maxBadges: 1 })[0] : undefined),
  [item, showBadges]
);

// Get rgba color for inverted corner box-shadow
const scoopColor = getBadgeScoopColor(badge.className);
// "bg-emerald-600/70 text-emerald-50" → "rgba(5, 150, 105, 0.7)"
```

#### Badge Types

| Category | Badges | Criteria |
|----------|--------|----------|
| **Recency** | `just-released`, `new`, `coming-soon`, `highly-anticipated` | Release date relative to today |
| **Popularity** | `viral`, `trending`, `very-popular` | TMDB popularity score + vote threshold |
| **Quality** | `all-time-great`, `critically-acclaimed`, `hidden-gem`, `really-bad` | Vote average + vote count |
| **Series** | `new-episode`, `new-season`, `currently-airing`, `mini-series`, `season-finale`, `series-finale`, `returning-soon` | Series status, episode air dates |
| **Movie** | `blockbuster`, `box-office-hit`, `indie` | Revenue, budget, rating |

#### Key Thresholds (`BADGE_THRESHOLDS`)

```typescript
BASE_VOTE_COUNT: 100,           // Min votes for most badges (prevents obscure items)
TRENDING_POPULARITY: 100,       // Min popularity for trending badge
VIRAL_POPULARITY: 1000,         // Min popularity for viral badge
ALL_TIME_GREAT_RATING: 8.0,     // Min rating + 10k votes
CRITICALLY_ACCLAIMED_RATING: 8.5, // Min rating + 5k votes
HIDDEN_GEM_RATING: 7.5,         // Good rating + low popularity
HIGHLY_ANTICIPATED_POPULARITY: 50, // For unreleased items only
```

#### Badge Visual Design

Badges appear inside the image at bottom-left with an **inverted corner** (Chrome tab style) effect:

```tsx
{badge && (
  <div className="absolute bottom-0 left-0 z-10 flex items-end">
    {/* Badge - small and sleek */}
    <span
      className={cn(
        "inline-flex items-center px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[9px] font-semibold",
        "rounded-tr-md",
        badge.className  // e.g., "bg-emerald-600/70 text-emerald-50"
      )}
    >
      {badge.shortLabel || badge.label}
    </span>
    {/* Inverted corner - creates smooth curve to image */}
    <div
      className="w-[6px] h-[6px] -ml-px"
      style={{
        background: "transparent",
        borderBottomLeftRadius: "6px",
        boxShadow: `-6px 6px 0 0 ${getBadgeScoopColor(badge.className)}`,
      }}
      aria-hidden="true"
    />
  </div>
)}
```

**Design specs:**
- Position: Inside image at bottom-left (`absolute bottom-0 left-0`)
- Size: Compact (`text-[9px] px-1.5 py-0.5`)
- Rounded: Top-right corner only (`rounded-tr-md`) - other corners touch image edges
- Colors: 70% opacity background for visibility (`bg-{color}-600/70 text-{color}-50`)
- **Inverted corner effect**: Uses the "box-shadow trick" - a transparent element with `border-bottom-left-radius` and a colored `box-shadow` that fills the curved area

**The inverted corner technique:**
1. A 6x6px transparent element sits next to the badge
2. It has a `border-bottom-left-radius` creating a quarter-circle cutout
3. A `box-shadow` extends from it, matching the badge color
4. This creates the illusion of the badge "curving into" the image

**getBadgeScoopColor utility** (`src/lib/badges/utils.ts`):
```tsx
// Maps badge className to rgba color for box-shadow
getBadgeScoopColor("bg-emerald-600/70 text-emerald-50")
// Returns: "rgba(5, 150, 105, 0.7)"
```

#### Card Height Consistency

Since badges are now inside the image (not below), card heights remain consistent regardless of badge presence:

```tsx
// Image container - always fully rounded
<div className="relative aspect-[2/3] overflow-hidden rounded-lg bg-muted">
  {/* ... image content ... */}
  
  {/* Badge inside image at bottom-left */}
  {badge && (
    <div className="absolute bottom-0 left-0 z-10 flex items-end">
      <span className={cn("...", badge.className)}>
        {badge.shortLabel || badge.label}
      </span>
      {/* Inverted corner element */}
      <div className="w-[6px] h-[6px] ..." />
    </div>
  )}
</div>

{/* Title - consistent margin (no badge-dependent spacing needed) */}
<div className="mt-2">
  <h3 className="text-sm font-medium line-clamp-1">{title}</h3>
</div>
```

#### Badge Priority

Badges are sorted by priority (lower = higher priority). When `maxBadges: 1` is set, only the highest priority badge is shown:

| Priority | Badge Types |
|----------|-------------|
| 0 | `just-released`, `new-episode` |
| 1 | `new`, `highly-anticipated`, `new-season` |
| 2 | `coming-soon`, `viral`, `series-finale` |
| 3 | `trending`, `season-finale` |
| 4 | `very-popular`, `returning-soon` |
| 5 | `all-time-great`, `currently-airing` |
| 6-8 | Quality & movie-specific badges |
| 99 | `really-bad` (lowest priority) |
| 100 | `watchlist`, `watched` (user status - shown separately in bottom-right) |

#### User Status Badges (Watchlist/Watched)

User status badges show in the **bottom-right** corner of cards (separate from content badges in bottom-left):

```tsx
import { UserStatusBadge, useIsWatched } from "@/components/features/media";

// In card components
<UserStatusBadge itemId={item.id} mediaType={mediaType} />

// Hook for grayscale effect on watched items
const isWatched = useIsWatched(item.id);
```

**Badge types:**
- `watchlist` - Shows "Saved" when item is in user's watchlist
- `watched` - Shows "Watched" when user has marked item as watched

**Visual design:**
- Neutral background: `bg-neutral-800/80 text-neutral-200`
- No icons (clean, minimal)
- Inverted corner scoop effect (mirrors content badge on left)
- Only shows one badge (priority: watched > watchlist)

**Grayscale effect for watched items:**
```tsx
// In card image
<Image
  className={cn(
    "object-cover",
    isWatched && "grayscale brightness-75 group-hover:grayscale-0 group-hover:brightness-100"
  )}
/>
```

**Hiding in context:**
Use `hideUserStatus` prop when the badge would be redundant (e.g., watchlist page):

```tsx
// On watchlist page - hide since user already knows these are in watchlist
<MediaCard item={movie} hideUserStatus />

// Also supported by MovieCard and WideMovieCard
<MovieCard item={movie} hideUserStatus />
```

#### Series Badge Logic

Series badges handle special cases:

```typescript
// Popularity badges take precedence over "currently-airing"
// If a show is trending/viral/very-popular, don't also show "Currently Airing"
const hasPopularityBadge = badges.some(
  (b) => b.type === "trending" || b.type === "very-popular" || b.type === "viral"
);
if (data.status === "Returning Series" && !hasPopularityBadge) {
  badges.push(createBadge("currently-airing"));
}

// Mini series: single season + ended status + optional keyword check
if (
  series.number_of_seasons === 1 &&
  series.status === "Ended" &&
  (hasKeyword(keywordIds, MINI_SERIES_KEYWORD_IDS) || true)
) {
  badges.push(createBadge("mini-series"));
}
```

#### Enabling Badges on Cards

```tsx
// MovieCard and WideMovieCard support showBadges prop
<MovieCard item={movie} showBadges />         // Default: true
<MovieCard item={movie} showBadges={false} /> // Disable badges

// MediaCard passes through
<MediaCard item={movie} showBadges />
```

### MediaCard Component (Card Display Preference)

The `MediaCard` component is a smart wrapper that renders either `MovieCard` (poster) or `WideMovieCard` (wide) based on the user's display preference stored in the preferences store.

```tsx
import { MediaCard, MediaCardSkeleton } from "@/components/features/movie/media-card";

// Basic usage - MediaCard reads preference internally
<MediaCard
  item={movie}
  className="w-[150px] flex-shrink-0"           // Size for poster mode
  wideClassName="w-[300px] flex-shrink-0"       // Size for wide mode
  showRating
  priority={index < 4}
/>

// With subtitle (character/job info for filmography)
<MediaCard
  item={movie}
  subtitle="Tony Stark / Iron Man"  // Shows below title in muted text
  showRating
/>

// Skeleton also respects preference
<MediaCardSkeleton className="w-[150px]" wideClassName="w-[300px]" />
```

**Props:**
- `item` - MovieListItem or SeriesListItem
- `className` - Sizing for poster mode
- `wideClassName` - Sizing for wide mode
- `showRating` - Show rating badge (default: true)
- `showBadges` - Show content badges like "New", "Trending" (default: true)
- `priority` - Image loading priority
- `enableHover` - Enable hover card (default: true on desktop)
- `subtitle` - Optional text below title (e.g., character name, job role)
- `hideUserStatus` - Hide watchlist/watched badge AND grayscale effect (use in watchlist/watched/ratings pages)

**Hiding user status indicators:**

Use `hideUserStatus={true}` when displaying content on user library pages where the status would be redundant or visually distracting:

```tsx
// On watchlist page - all items are already in watchlist
<MediaCard item={movie} hideUserStatus />

// On watched page - all items are already watched (also disables grayscale)
<MediaCard item={movie} hideUserStatus />

// On ratings page - showing liked/disliked items
<MediaCard item={movie} hideUserStatus />
```

When `hideUserStatus` is true:
1. User status badge (bottom-right "Saved"/"Watched") is hidden
2. Grayscale effect on watched items is disabled (posters show full color)

**Key patterns:**
- `MediaCard` internally uses `usePreferencesStore(selectCardDisplayMode)` to decide which card to render
- Always provide both `className` (poster sizing) and `wideClassName` (wide sizing) for responsive display
- Grids need to change column count for wide mode (fewer columns for wider cards)

**Grid layout changes for wide mode:**
```tsx
const displayMode = usePreferencesStore(selectCardDisplayMode);

// Poster: more columns, smaller cards
const posterGridClass = "grid grid-cols-3 sm:grid-cols-4 md:grid-cols-5 lg:grid-cols-6 xl:grid-cols-7 gap-2.5";

// Wide: fewer columns, larger cards
const wideGridClass = "grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 xl:grid-cols-5 gap-4";

<div className={displayMode === "wide" ? wideGridClass : posterGridClass}>
  {items.map((item) => <MediaCard key={item.id} item={item} />)}
</div>
```

**Scroller sizing patterns:**
```tsx
// Poster card sizing in scrollers
const posterCardClass = "w-[120px] sm:w-[135px] md:w-[150px] lg:w-[160px] flex-shrink-0";

// Wide card sizing in scrollers
const wideCardClass = "w-[220px] sm:w-[260px] md:w-[300px] lg:w-[340px] flex-shrink-0";
```

**WideMovieCard image fallback chain:**
1. CDN `widePoster` → `https://image.themoviebrowser.com/{type}/{id}/widePoster.webp`
2. CDN `backdrop` → `https://image.themoviebrowser.com/{type}/{id}/backdrop.webp`
3. TMDB `backdrop` → `https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780{backdrop_path}`

